terabyte HANA databases

00:14:04.320 --> 00:14:08.460
and scale out to 64 terabytes
using HPE Superdome.

00:14:08.460 --> 00:14:10.590
So this enables the
largest enterprises

00:14:10.590 --> 00:14:13.320
to run the biggest
SAP environments

00:14:13.320 --> 00:14:16.500
on bare-metal connected to GCP.

00:14:16.500 --> 00:14:18.180
In certain instances,
you can even

00:14:18.180 --> 00:14:22.080
run part of your SAP landscape
in GCP connecting to that HANA

00:14:22.080 --> 00:14:25.170
or maybe underlying
Oracle database that

00:14:25.170 --> 00:14:27.000
manages that data in SAP.

00:14:27.000 --> 00:14:30.690
Depending on those applications
and how they perform,

00:14:30.690 --> 00:14:32.890
we see customers doing that.

00:14:32.890 --> 00:14:34.390
So that's an interesting option.

00:14:34.390 --> 00:14:38.395
And again, the idea is we're
getting your data into GCP

00:14:38.395 --> 00:14:40.770
so that you can leverage all
the great things are on data

00:14:40.770 --> 00:14:42.845
analytics that GCP enables.

00:14:42.845 --> 00:14:44.300
